  "summary": "Validates the `inputs` argument in the `sendall` RPC to reject duplicate outpoints. An RPC error (RPC_INVALID_PARAMETER) is returned if the caller supplies the same UTXO more than once.",
  "problem": "When duplicate inputs are passed to `sendall`, the wallet sums the input value repeatedly and creates an invalid transaction containing duplicate inputs. The resulting transaction fails mempool acceptance with `bad-txns-inputs-duplicate` but remains committed in the local wallet, locking the affected UTXO and causing negative balance reporting until manually abandoned.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author provides reproduction on regtest: running `sendall '[\"<addr>\"]' '{\"inputs\": [<utxo>, <utxo>]}'` creates an invalid transaction with double the output value that fails mempool validation with `bad-txns-inputs-duplicate` and produces `nonmempool: -1.0` in `getbalances`.",
    "Author notes other RPCs like `send` avoid this because `CCoinControl::Select` deduplicates inputs, whereas `sendall` did not."
  ],
